It is normal, okay and expected to lose lots of games of nethack
before your first ascension. However, if your stated goal is to
ascend, you should be moving closer to that goal (as measured by which
milestones -- mines, soko, quest, medusa, castle, etc. -- you reach,
and how reliably) over the relatively short term. 

If your performance, averaged over the last dozen or so games, is not
showing visible forward progress, I suggest you reconsider your
approach. Every lost game carries a lesson, and mere persistence will
avail you nothing if you do not learn those lessons and take them to
heart. Practically all nethack deaths are preventable -- perhaps not
the immediate cause, but the root causes leading up to the situation
in which death was inescapable.

OTOH, if you are just enjoying playing around and really don't care
if you should ever ascend or not, then happy hacking. 


